      {
        "id": 120100,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-05T04:11:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jcubela2\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/f4b2a3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jcubela2:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does the ongoing effect of a card effect only the hero using it, or all heroes?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br>Depends on the card.<br><br>Tempest's Otherworldly Resilience only provides DR to him.&nbsp; But Shielding Winds provides every hero with DR from instances of 5+ damage (that's a single instance of damage, so \"5 (type) damage\", not \"five total damage from one source in a turn (1,3,1/2,2,1/3,2/1,1,1,1,1/etc.)\").&nbsp; However, Legacy's Superhuman Durability only reduces damage to him, as it specifies (but it provides more DR!).<br><br>If a card says \"Increase all damage dealt by 1\" then all damage is increased.&nbsp; Villain, hero, and environment; be it from a target, one-shot, or abstract source like \"the environment\".&nbsp; \"Increase damage dealt by villain targets by 1\", however, increases damage dealt by any villain card that has HP (as a target is a card with HP).<br><br>Hope this helps!</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:29.178Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11489,
        "topic_slug": "nube-question-about-ongoing",
        "display_username": "Reckless",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"jcubela2\"]\n\nDoes the ongoing effect of a card effect only the hero using it, or all heroes?\n\n[/quote]\n<br />Depends on the card.<br /><br />Tempest&#39;s Otherworldly Resilience only provides DR to him.&nbsp; But Shielding Winds provides every hero with DR from instances of 5+ damage (that&#39;s a single instance of damage, so &quot;5 (type) damage&quot;, not &quot;five total damage from one source in a turn (1,3,1/2,2,1/3,2/1,1,1,1,1/etc.)&quot;).&nbsp; However, Legacy&#39;s Superhuman Durability only reduces damage to him, as it specifies (but it provides more DR!).<br /><br />If a card says &quot;Increase all damage dealt by 1&quot; then all damage is increased.&nbsp; Villain, hero, and environment; be it from a target, one-shot, or abstract source like &quot;the environment&quot;.&nbsp; &quot;Increase damage dealt by villain targets by 1&quot;, however, increases damage dealt by any villain card that has HP (as a target is a card with HP).<br /><br />Hope this helps!\n",
